WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:04.373
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.373 --> 00:00:06.370
- [Dr. Mike] Hey everybody! Dr. Mike here.

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:07.960
Everyone has their morning routine,

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.690
and I'd like to show you what mine is like

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.700
to prepare me for a hectic
day in the hospital.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:13.230
The first thing I like
to do in the morning

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:16.520
when I open my eyes, is to grab
a glass of warm lemon water.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.610
The warm water allows
your digestive system to

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.450
improve its circulation and
get ready to start the day.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.670
Also, lemons contain two great nutrients,

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.140
potassium and a little bit of vitamin C,

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:28.500
which is great, especially
if the night before

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:29.880
you had a great workout or

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.470
maybe even had an extra drink of alcohol

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:32.870
that you shouldn't have had.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:41.013
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.490
The second thing I like to do when

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.840
I wake up in the morning is make my bed.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.160
It sounds like a small task,

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:51.290
but your brain loves
achieving goals big or small,

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:54.000
and setting a small goal
that is easily achievable

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.960
allows your brain to set bigger
goals throughout the day.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.100
Most importantly,

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.313
who doesn't like coming
home to a clean bed?

00:01:01.722 --> 00:01:02.555
Rox,

00:01:02.555 --> 00:01:03.388
Come on,

00:01:03.388 --> 00:01:04.221
you're late with the fives.

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.000
A great trick to waking up in the morning,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.560
that is even better than caffeine,

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:14.210
is to take a cold shower.

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:15.610
You don't need to take a full cold shower,

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:17.560
you can start with warm and move up

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:19.140
and do 10 seconds of cold.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.860
Just like this.

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.710
Science says it could
even improve testosterone

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.256
and improve circulation and focus.

00:01:25.256 --> 00:01:26.089
AAAAHH!

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:34.880
Gotta get dressed,

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:35.930
that's a no brainer,

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:36.960
everyone is doing it.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.560
Sometimes I'll need to wear scrubs

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:39.990
if I'm working the Emergency Room

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.550
or the Obstetric Department.

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:43.310
Sometimes I'll need to put on a suite

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.520
if I'm doing a formal presentation,

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.160
or seeing patients inside my clinic.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:50.020
I like my scrubs to be very fitted.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.170
A lot about being a doctor is
about your non-verbal cues,

00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.290
how you present yourself.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:57.300
I also like my scrubs to
be bright colored, happy,

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.470
and really show that confident energy that

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.820
I like to give to my
patients every single day.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.010
Another crucial part of my morning routine

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:11.330
is an easy five minute warm up.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.700
I'm not telling you to do
a full exercise regimen

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:14.533
when you wake up,

00:02:14.533 --> 00:02:16.810
but take a few minutes,
move your body around,

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:19.160
it will do wonders for your concentration,

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:20.047
your flexibility,

00:02:20.047 --> 00:02:22.373
and most importantly,
it will prevent injury.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.340
My favorite part of the morning is

00:02:30.340 --> 00:02:32.660
taking this little husky out for a walk.

00:02:32.660 --> 00:02:35.370
Roxy obviously needs her
daily morning exercise,

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.770
but it's also a great time for me

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:38.220
to do some self reflection,

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.870
leave my cell phone behind,
enjoy the beauty of the city,

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.200
maybe get a little vitamin
D if it's sunny out,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.320
but ultimately I find
that walk is a great way

00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.013
for me to meditate and get
ready for the rest of my day.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.710
Last but not least, got
to get some food in me

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.530
before I head out to the hospital.

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.540
Proteins, complex carbohydrates,

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.220
great ways to start your day.

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:03.320
Get some eggs, whole wheat
bread, maybe some oatmeal,

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.300
leave you feeling full and energized

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.970
throughout your entire work day.

00:03:06.970 --> 00:03:09.510
I also like to grab a
quick snack like a banana,

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:11.230
get some vitamins in,

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:12.760
because the hospital can be a crazy place

00:03:12.760 --> 00:03:13.910
you need a quick snack.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.340
So, I'm ready to start my day.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.350
If you do something interesting
in your morning routine

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:23.730
that you would like to share with me,

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:24.810
leave it in the comments.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:26.360
If there is something you
would like to know more

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.450
about your morning routine,

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:28.680
leave it in the comments.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.550
If you haven't hit subscribe already,

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:31.663
hit that button now.

